    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "51b4324c_787fcf32",
        "filename": "drivers/mmc/host/mtk-sd.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2205,
      "author": {
        "id": 1409360
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-17T11:18:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ya, sdus_mask should\u0027t be meaningless of cause, but MTK old chipsets had a non-cqe （aka SW-cqe，used software to simulate HW-cqe）solution, those old chipsets will be also updated to GKI version in future, so we must take care of non-cqe requirement.\n\ncrypto engine of MTK non-cqe solution is not a standard part of eMMC, so crypto engine is special which is very different with cqe HW setting.\n\nso, \"non_cqe\" string in my patch is only for MTK chipset, it\u0027s not a standard path.",
      "parentUuid": "b3050927_bdb3a6b6",
      "revId": "77ae4e2b579dff29039c9277e28b892d76fc014a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
